A||||14||WKDFIRO||Junkyard Ranting....||||8||
Z||000000||WKDFIRO||04-17-2001||03:44 AM||||A few days ago I was at the Pick-A-Part yard and ran into an 87 GT that had just been put down. It actually looked in great condition...too good to be here in the yard...but I got out the headlight motors that I needed and some other odds and ends but didn't have enough money to get the real cherry stuff. Flawless tail lights, relatively good looking body panels all the way around, good looking steering wheel and of all things, under the seat covers 2 PERFECT GREY FIERO GT SEATS. I laughed because the seats were actually bolted onto metal plates raising them an inch higher! I thought about getting them but since I have an 85 GT with speakers they wouldn't do me much and I didn't have the money to get either one. So I figured, oh well, someone will get them and put them to good use. Thats the way this game is played. I would come back and it would be picked clean, so I thought.<P>I went back today and I don't think I can overstate how this GT was RAPED. Door panels weren't unbolted they were PRYED off. Radio/AC plates were BROKEN off. The center console was bent in half and thrown in the trunk. The auto shifter plates also BROKEN. The gauge pod was pried open and the gauges ripped out. In the front, the carrier for the sunroof was broken in half and useless to anyone. Then something caught my eye in the trunk of the car beside me:<P>THE GT SEATS WERE TORN OPEN AND SMEARED WITH GREASE AND OIL!!! THEY WERE RUINED!!!! I COULDN'T BELIEVE MY EYES.<P>My mouth hung open for what seemed to be a long time. Of all the things they got off the car they broke everything else and ruined the rest. The body panels that weren't broken were scratched to hell, Greasy, oily parts of other cars were simply thrown in to the ruins of the interior as if to further insult the Fiero. <P>Now I feel horrible that I didn't get everything out that I know that others may have needed. I would have taken my time all day unbolting and taking care of these scarce parts that we Fiero owners care about.<P>Please tell me that Im not the only one here not simply OUTRAGED by this....this...VIOLATION of a Fiero!||||reg||8
Z||000001||Mattsfiero||04-17-2001||07:49 AM||||For me junkyard trips are a common thing. Especially seeing I have alot to do to rebuild mine. It amazes me there is only a couple of known fieros in my neck of the woods but they are the first thing torn through in the yards. And when I say torn I mean TORN. I am always as careful as I can be when removing something just in case somebody else needs the part. Some people just don't care. What about the parts I have needed but where destroyed. It just isn't right or fair for that matter. What can we say or do for that matter. Just keep doing what we have.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Matt<BR>85 custom coupe<BR>Mattsfiero@aol.com<BR>www.anglefire.com/ma3/mattsfiero||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||04-17-2001||08:50 AM||||That's aweful  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I have a story that might cheer ya up.  Last summer a local shop had a bare bones rough looking black '85 Fiero that was abandoned on the e-way and towed to his shop.  If nobody claimed the car in 60 days or something, he would be stuck with it.  The shop owner asked me if I wanted it since he knew I was working on mine at the time.  I could have picked it up cheap but had no room for it.  Well eventually the Fiero went to the junkyard, but the shop owner told me the junkyard owner's son took the car, got it running and was using it as a daily driver.||||reg||1
Z||000003||firstfiero||04-17-2001||09:40 AM||||      Dude that junkyard I just went to that had 50 fieros was the same way...It looked like a wrecking ball went through them. It doesn't make any sense...destroy the interior and you throw away money!<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif"> <BR>Todd <BR>  86se||||reg||13
Z||000004||TheFiero64||04-17-2001||10:11 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mattsfiero:<BR><B>For me junkyard trips are a common thing. Especially seeing I have alot to do to rebuild mine. It amazes me there is only a couple of known fieros in my neck of the woods but they are the first thing torn through in the yards. And when I say torn I mean TORN. I am always as careful as I can be when removing something just in case somebody else needs the part. Some people just don't care. What about the parts I have needed but where destroyed. It just isn't right or fair for that matter. What can we say or do for that matter. Just keep doing what we have.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your not kidding, remember when we went to self serve and found an 88 shift console that would be mint if it wasn't smashed by the hood.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg"> <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
