Z||000008||phreakboy4||04-17-2001||06:28 PM||||yeah I was just in a junkyard and found a nice condition 86 se that had an excellent interior until the yard let their dog live in it and **** all over everything and chew on everything, just incase anyone need one, I found a really good condition tan dash<P>84 2M4 coupe(phreakboy45@cs.com)   Sean V||||reg||1
Z||000009||KissMySSFiero||04-17-2001||09:30 PM||||at first i thought this was going to be a post of someone ranting about how people have been posting there finds.  i feel the same as all of you.  the ones that seem to be the worst are the yards that charge admission.  2 bucks to get in and everything in the yard has a fixed price regardless of condition.  if ever see a fiero in a yard thats in good condition im going to talk to the owner of the place and ask if hell put it aside so i can be the one to rape it.  ill get everything i can..if i cant just get the whole thing.  and ill try to get the parts to people who need them.  i just moved to where im at now and i havent seen much of this.  i hope i find one soon that i can part out.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
Z||000010||KissMySSFiero||04-17-2001||09:33 PM||||also the reason yards dont let people in to pull their own parts is this exactly.  the people who break stuff out rather than removing it the right way.  one yard i used to go to flat out told me that(even though its obvious)  he set a fiero aside for me when i asked because he didnt want this to happen.  but then he wanted to much for the parts so i told him not to worry about it.  im sure that car has been beat to death by now.  <P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>     <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>      <P>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">          <BR>"When in Doubt..Whip it out!!"||||reg||1
Z||000011||fierofreek2001||04-18-2001||12:10 AM||||i have a similar situation of total fiero raping... i sold my coupe that i treated like my own child to a kid ... well i should have thought twice about selling it because 2 weeks later he wrecked it, and then decided that since it wasnt goin to be road worthy anymore, he might as well take a SLEDGE HAMMER TO IT , rip the windshield wipers off, knife the seats, bash in all the platic exterior panels, tear out the dash , break the windows , rip off the hood, spray paint yellow paint all over the place... total annihalation... the sad thing was that the engine was just rebuilt, and i had put all my GOOD fiero parts into the car because i was driving it daily before i sold it... well all that crap down the drain because of a friggin dumbass that had nothing better to do then destroy a piece of rare history... DAMN IT!<BR>oh and we also picked up an indy fiero that was totally destroyed too, it sat for 2 years, and water leaked in the sunroof... seat covers and original seats got all moldy, the kid painted the doors BLACK and the carpeting on the floor... they tore the wing off... man i hate morons.. i wish there were more people with sense enough to understand what they have is rare and that they can't just go out and buy another one... <BR>oh well .. thank god for this forum and all these cool people, so we can preserve what we have left!!!<P>steve||||reg||1
